quests.description:
10 Obsidian in this pattern (2 on top and bottom, 3 for sides).
{image:atm:textures/questpics/gettingstarted/example_netherportal.png width:150 height:200 align:center}
Then, light it on Fire and we'll light up The Nether Portal. Walking through it will Teleport us to The Nether. \n\nA Dimension full of Lava, Fire, and angry Mobs.

To upgrade Allthemodium to Vibranium you will need another Smithing Template. 
This one you can find by Brushing Suspicious Soul Sand. 

Which is found in Bastions in The Nether.

{image:atm:textures/questpics/allthemodium/all_bastion.png width:200 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/allthemodium/all_soul.png width:200 height:100 align:center}

One thing that bugs many Modded Players is that Enchanting can't be completely automated! And you can't choose which Enchants you want, you have to get Lucky! \n\nWell don't worry both those wishes have been fulfilled! With the Runic Enchanter. \n\nTo use it, you won't have to touch the Enchanting Table, just pipe in the right Items, Source, and XP Fluid. \n\nXP Fluid will need to be obtained by bottling some form of Liquid XP with the Bottling Machine from Immersive Engineering, then processing it through Extended Industrialization Canning Machine. \n\nYou'll need to make Infused Dragon's Breath and Mending Books to remake the ATM Star!
{@pagebreak}
(Light Blue Carpet is Soul-Touched Deepshelf
Purple Carpet is Echoing Sculkshelf
Blue Carpet is Soul-Touched Sculkshelf)
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_enchanter1.png width:125 height:100 align:center}
The base of the Runic Enchanter is full of practically everything! It has Darkstone galore, Bookshelves, Rune Blocks, and Arcane Crystal Blocks!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_enchanter2.png width:125 height:100 align:center}
We will continue in a similar way, just replace our Rune Blocks and Arcane Crystal Blocks with Gilded Chiseled Polished Darkstone and Darkstone Pillars. Yeah those new looking funny squares are the tops of Darkstone Pillars!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_enchanter3.png width:125 height:100 align:center}
Don't worry it is getting easier! Keep a few more Bookshelves as well as adding Darkstone Pedestals and an Enchanting Table.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_enchanter4.png width:125 height:100 align:center}
Heck this one is even easier! Just 4 Soul Lanterns on top of the last Bookshelves.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_enchanter5.png width:125 height:100 align:center}
Okay this one is too easier! Just place a Quantum Injector a Block above the Enchanting Table.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_enchanter6.png width:150 height:150 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_enchanter7.png width:150 height:150 align:center}
Probably should have told you earlier but the Hatches go in the Bottom of the Runic Enchanter... sorry!

One of the most important Mutliblocks, mostly because we need it for the other Multiblocks. \n\nHere you'll need Fluid Input (each Input can only hold 1 type of Fluid so you'll need multiple), Energy Input, and Item Input and Output Hatches. \n\nUsing those Hatches we can input all the Items, Fluids, and Energy and it'll craft our Items, like the other Multiblock Controllers! \n\nOr craft our Items needed for the Star Parts! You'll need a lot of Blood, Aureal, Souls, and Energy for them!
{@pagebreak}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_forge1.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
First layer is pretty simple. Just some Polished Darkstone Blocks and Stairs. Along with the Rune Blocks and Arcane Polished Darkstone. Oh wait, I almost forgot the most important Block! The Forge Block
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_forge2.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
Next layer will have more Darkstone in Blocks, Stairs, and Slabs and even Gilded Arcane Polished Darkstone and Chiseled Polished Arcane Darkstone. Can't forget the 4 Arcane Crystal Obelisks!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_forge3.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
This one's very easy! Just a Tier 5 Forge square in the center with 8 Darkstone Pedestals 2 Blocks away from it.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_forge4.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
We're going to skip a layer because nothing is added there! Instead, with a Block of space between them. Place the Quantum Injector above the Tier 5 Forge.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_forge5.png width:200 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_forge6.png width:200 height:100 align:center}
Last is placing a few more Hatches! We'll need them!

Alright another Multiblock! This one requiring more ports than any Naval Base has seen!\n\nWe'll need Fluid Input and Output hatches and Item Input and Output hatches.\n\nNow, this ends up being a bit of a process so follow along carefully!\n\nFirst, we'll need Unrefined Liquid Souls which comes from using a Fluid Extractor (from IF) on a Soul Tree.\n\nNext, we need Liquefied Source which we can get using a Source Condenser. A Source Condenser will pull Source from nearby Source Jars and turn it into Liquefied Source!\n\nThen, we can use the Runic Crucible to combine Souls, Unrefined Liquid Souls, and Liquefied Source together into Liquid Souls!\n\nFinally, we'll use the Liquid Souls, Liquefied Source, and some items from Mekanism to craft Obsidiansteel.
{@pagebreak}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_crucible1.png width:125 height:100 align:center}
First layer of the Runic Crucible has a Gilded Chiseled Polished Darkstone in the middle, around it is Polished Darkstone. Then, on the sides we'll have upside down Polished Darkstone Stairs, with Rune Blocks on the corners.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_crucible2.png width:125 height:100 align:center}
Smack dab in the middle we'll put an Arcane Crystal with Polished Darkstone Stairs around it. On the sides will be Arcane Polished Darkstone Pillars, Polished Darkstone which will be replaced by Hatches, and Arcane Polished Darkstone.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_crucible3.png width:125 height:100 align:center}
Just place Arcane Crystal Blocks on each corner and call it a day!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_crucible4.png width:125 height:100 align:center}
Finally, with a block of space, place the Quantum Injector above the middle Arcane Crystal Block.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_crucible5.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/chap3/creative_crucible6.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
The Polished Darkstone blocks in the middle layer are where we'll place our Hatches!

The single most important! Most powerful! Most dangerous Artifact of them all!
{@pagebreak}
I'm not even sure if I should explain what it does, it's too dangerous!
{@pagebreak}
If you're so sure you can handle its power, then maybe keep reading...
{@pagebreak}
Not too late to turn back!
{@pagebreak}
Okay I warned you...
{@pagebreak}
Press Shift for a chance to Fart when Whoopie Cushion is equipped.

Put an Importer onto the inventory you want stuff pulled from. Next, put the Interface on the second inventory and connect them with Logic Cables. Then, put in the Variable Card into the Importer and change it as you please.\n\nIt can be changed to import things at the Integer Limit (Over 2 billion).
{image:atm:textures/questpics/logistics/id_item.png width:200 height:50 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/logistics/id_fluid.png width:200 height:50 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/logistics/id_energy.png width:200 height:50 align:center}

Hostile Neural Networks (HNN for short) is a mod based around simulating mob kills for loot!

To do this, you will be collecting "data" on mobs, then running simulations from the data to create their drops!

{image:atm:textures/questpics/hnn.png width:150 height:150 align:center}

Tier 2 needs 6 Draconium Ingot Blocks, 1 on each side of the Core. Then, obviously the 4 Stabilizers to be made.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_2off.png width:100 height:100 align:1}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_2on.png width:100 height:100 align:1}

Last and the best one Tier 8! You'll need 378 Awakened Draconium Blocks and 786 Draconium Ingot Blocks! Is it worth it?
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_8off.png width:100 height:100 align:1}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_8on.png width:100 height:100 align:1}

Tier 1 only needs the Core and 4 Stabilizers to be made.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_1off.png width:100 height:100 align:1}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_1on.png width:100 height:100 align:1}

Tier 3 needs 26 Draconium Ingot Blocks around it, fully encasing the Core, to be made.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_3off.png width:100 height:100 align:1}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_3on.png width:100 height:100 align:1}

Almost there! Tier 7. 210 Draconium Ingots and 328 Redstone Blocks!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_7off.png width:100 height:100 align:1}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_7on.png width:100 height:100 align:1}

Tier 4 is different. First, it needs 26 Redstone Blocks encasing the Core. Then above the Redstone it needs 56 Draconium Ingot Blocks.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_4off.png width:100 height:100 align:1}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_4on.png width:100 height:100 align:1}

The Reactor Core is the most important part of the Reactor, IE the Core! Place it 5 blocks or more from the Injector and Stabilizers, and you can right click it to see it's GUI here you'll find a few bars, a ball, buttons, and slots. The Bars go from left to right: Heat, Containment Field, Energy Saturation, and Fuel Conversion. You already learned about the Field and Energy and you will learn about the Fuel in a next quest. So the Heat is pretty important as when warming up it will raise to 2000C before being ready to activate. Make sure it doesn't get too high or else... meltdown! The Ball is the image of your Core, right now I have a bug where the Core doesn't have a texture so I can't explain much. The Buttons change the appearance of GUI, to activate or shutdown the Reactor, and charge it.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_reactor_off_down.png width:200 height:100 align:1}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_reactor_off_up.png width:150 height:150 align:1}

500 Million OP? Check. Fuel? Check. Heat at 2000 C? Check. Just click that activate button and pray it doesn't Meltdown!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_reactor_on_down.png width:200 height:100 align:1}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_reactor_on_up.png width:150 height:150 align:1}

Tier 6 needs 150 Draconium Ingot Blocks and 178 Redstone Blocks (Don't forget 36 Stabilizers).
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_6off.png width:100 height:100 align:1}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_6on.png width:100 height:100 align:1}

Tier 5 needs 90 Draconium Ingot Blocks and 80 Redstone Blocks, along with 4 Advanced Stabilizers or 36 Stabilizers.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_5off.png width:100 height:100 align:1}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/draconic/draconic_core_5on.png width:100 height:100 align:1}

Coke Oven is how we make our Coal Coke, take a guess what it's made of! \n\nWe can use the Oven to smelt Logs into Charcoal, or smelt Coal and Coal Blocks into Coke! \n\nEither of these will produce Creosote Oil as well as the normal recipe.
{@pagebreak}
The Coke Oven is a very simple Multiblock, 3x3x3 of Coke Bricks.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_coke1.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_coke2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_coke3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Simply Right Click the Middle Block of the Front Side with an Engineer's Hammer to create it.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_coke.png width:100 height:100 align:center}

Alloys are combinations of 2 different Metals. \n\nMetals aren't usually liquid at room temperature so we'll need to smelt them a bit (thanks Mercury)! \n\nAdd the 2 Metals into the top slots, and a Furnace Fuel like Charcoal into the bottom slot. \n\nWait... Steel is an Alloy!
{@pagebreak}
The Alloy Kiln is a 2x2x2 of Kiln Bricks.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_alloy1.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_alloy2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Then Right Click the Top Right Block with an Engineer's Hammer to make it!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_alloy.png width:100 height:100 align:center}

The Crude Blast Furnace is our very simple (and crude) way of producing Steel. \n\nYou'll need to feed it an Iron Ingot and either Charcoal or Coke. \n\nEach Steel Ingot takes 60 seconds to bake. Charcoal gives us 15 seconds while Coke gives us the whole 60 seconds. These can also be multiplied with their Block forms. \n\nWe also get Slag... it's pretty useless.
{@pagebreak}
This one is another 3x3x3, just now with Blast Bricks.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_crude1.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_crude2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_crude3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Another time where we Right Click the Front Middle Block with our trusty Hammer!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_crude.png width:100 height:100 align:center}

The Silo is a Multiblock made for storing tons of just one type of Item, like a Drawer. \n\nYou can deposit the Item and its duplicates in the Top Side or Bottom Side, but to extract you'll need to use the Bottom Side! \n\nIt can hold 41,472 Items, just only of the same type.
{@pagebreak}
First we place a square of Treated Wood Fences with an Iron Sheetmetal in the center.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_silo1.png width:125 height:100 align:center}
Next, we make a full square of Iron Sheetmetal above our Fences, while leaving a space in the center hollow. Do this 5 times!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_silo2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_silo3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_silo4.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_silo5.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_silo6.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Then, the final layer which is an entire square of Iron Sheetmetal, including us filling in the center Block.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_silo7.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
After that, Right Click the Middle Iron Sheetmetal on the second layer with our Hammer to create our Silo!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_silo.png width:100 height:125 align:center}

The Tank is just like the Silo but for Fluids! \n\nIt can hold only 1 type of Fluid, but it can hold 512 Buckets of that Fluid. \n\nYou can Input Fluid from the Top or Bottom Side, but you can only Output from the Bottom.
{@pagebreak}
The Tank is built similar to the Silo, start with our Treated Fences and singular Iron Sheetmetal.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_tank1.png width:125 height:100 align:center}
Now we build our hollow squares of Iron Sheetmetals above our Fences, this time 3 Blocks high.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_tank2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_tank3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_tank4.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Then, top it off with a filled in square of Iron Sheetmetal!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_tank5.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Right Click the same Block as in the Silo to create our Tank.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_tank.png width:100 height:120 align:center}

Trust me the Multiblock ain't lying when it says it's improved! \n\nThis one can be automated to recieve Inputs from the Top, and Outputs from the Front and Back Slots. \n\nAlso, we can add Preheaters to its Left and Right! \n\nAll this makes it much faster and of course, more efficient!
{@pagebreak}
Finally a different one! You'll start with a base of 3x3x3 Reinforced Blast Bricks.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_blast1.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_blast2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_blast3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Then, place a Hopper on the Top of the Middle Block.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_blast4.png width:100 height:125 align:center}
Now Right Click the Middle Block of the 2nd layer with the Engineer's Hammer.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_blast.png width:100 height:150 align:center}

This is the Generator you will most likely be using, the Diesel Generator! \n\nYou will Input Fuel in the bottom left and right corners of the Diesel Generator. The Fuel can be: Creasote Oil, Biodiesel, and High-Cetane Biodiesel. Those are in order from worst to best! \n\nThe Diesel Generator will burn the Fuel and produce Energy which can be Output from the 3 connectors in the front.
{@pagebreak}
In the back of the Diesel Generator we'll need 3 Radiator Blocks. The middle will be Fluid Pipes surrounded by Steel Scaffolding. With the front having a Generator Block and 2 Fluid Pipes next to it.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_diesel1.png width:100 height:150 align:center}
Above the 3 Radiator Blocks will be 3 more Radiator Blocks! And the Generator Block and Fluid Pipes next to it, will have 3 Generator Blocks above them. The rest will be filled with Heavy Engineering Blocks and a single Redstone Engineering Block.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_diesel2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
To finish we'll need 3 more Radiator Blocks above the other ones, and next to it we'll make a cross of Heavy Engineering Blocks.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_diesel3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Last step is to Right Click the middle and top Generator Block with our Engineer's Hammer!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_diesel.png width:100 height:100 align:center}

After building the Lightning Coil we can have Lightning Strike the Steel Fences, which will then become Energy in its own Energy reservoir. \n\nThe more Steel Fences the higher chance of Lightning! \n\nI wonder if we can use other Mods to summon Lightning?
{@pagebreak}
To harness the power of Mother Nature's most devastating we'll need to start with a High-Voltage Coil Block. Then, place HV Accumulators adjacent to the High-Voltage Coil Block. On the corners place down Steel Scaffolding.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_lightning1.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
For the next layer, place another High-Voltage Coil Block on top of the previous one. Adjacent to that one, will be Light Engineering Blocks. On the corners will just be simple Treated Fences!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_lightning2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Now, we need a third High-Voltage Coil Blocks above the others, and surrounding it will be 8 Copper Coil Blocks.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_lightning3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Then, Right Click the Light Engineering Block on the Front Side with a Hammer to convert it to the Lightning Coil!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_lightning.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
I didn't make a picture for this step but you will need Steel Fences on top of the Lightning Coil in order to get Lightning to hit it!

The Metal Press is our Best Friend for all Crafting Recipes with Metal! \n\nIt's very simple, we place our Molds onto the Press, attach some Energy to the top, and toss our Items onto the Conveyor Belts. \n\nOur Items will pass through, get Pressed, and become a new Item that keeps moving on the Belt! \n\nThese can be used to make Wires, Plates, Rods, and... Melon Slices?
{@pagebreak}
First layer is very simple, just Steel Scaffolding and both sides of a Redstone Enginerring Block.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_press1.png width:150 height:75 align:center}
Next, we place a Piston, facing Down, above the Redstone Engineering Block and add two Conveyor Belts next to it.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_press2.png width:125 height:100 align:center}
Then, we place a single Heavy Engineering Block above our Piston!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_press3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Last, we Right Click the Piston with the Engineer's Hammer!

The Crusher is a very dangerous and loud Machine. \n\nYou can Input Items (or Mobs) into the Top Grates, and it will Crush them into their Drops! \n\nThis can be very helpful especially with taking Raw Ores into Dust. If we use Raw Ore Blocks it will give us more Dust than what the Hammer will give, also some have a chance at giving an entirely new type of Dust! \n\nAll the Drops will come out of the Bottom Front Block, automatically ejecting. It will also need Energy Input from the Top Right Side.
{@pagebreak}
The Crusher is pretty big, we'll need to place this layout of Steel Scaffolding and Light Engineering Blocks. The direction the Light Engineering Blocks face is the Front side!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_crusher1.png width:100 height:150 align:center}
On top of our 3 Light Engineering Blocks we'll place 3 more. We'll also place a Redstone Engineering Block and Light Engineering Block on the Left Side. Then, put another Light Block in the middle and surround it with Steel Fences.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_crusher2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Finally, we just throw 9 Hoppers on top of the Steel Fences and in the middle!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_crusher3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
You'll need to smack the middle Fence to make the Multiblock.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_crusher.png width:100 height:100 align:center}

The Sawmill works similar to the Metal Press, using Conveyor Belts and needing extra Items. \n\nIt works in 2 stages, first it Strips the Logs. If it doesn't have a Sawblade within it, it will only Strip Logs. Second stage is cutting the Log into Planks, this needs a Sawblade. \n\nSawblades are Crafted with a ton of Steel. They have Durability and to insert them, Right Click the Slots near the Back of the Sawmill. If you wish to take them out, turn off the Sawmill with Redstone, then Shift Right Click where you inserted them. \n\nYou'll need to give it Energy on the Top of the Back Side, and you can Input Items via the Conveyor Belts. The Items will Output with those same Belts, but the Sawdust comes out of a Port in Front of the Machine.
{@pagebreak}
Make an I shape with Steel Scaffolding (don't forget the Heavy Engineering Block) and fill in one part with Light Engineering Blocks and the other with Iron Sheetmetal.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_saw1.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
Place 3 more Light Engineering Blocks on their lower comrades. Add 1 Iron Sheetmetal on the Left most Iron Sheetmetal and next to it place a Redstone Engineering Block. Next to top Iron Sheetmetal we'll need another Heavy Engineering Block. Don't forget to add the Conveyor Belts, these are needed to Build it!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_saw2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Right Click the middle Iron Sheetmetal with our Hammer!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_saw.png width:100 height:100 align:center}

The Mixer is just like the ones your Mother/Grandmother uses to mix eggs into flour and sugar to bake whatever delicious treat they are making! \n\nThe Mixer will mix Items and Fluids. To get Fluids in we'll need to use the Port on the Left Side of the Mixer. To give it Items we'll need to use the Ports at the back. \n\nIn order to work it'll need Energy put into it from the Port at the Top of the Front of the Mixer. \n\nOnce it mixes, our result will come out the Port in the Front of the Machine!
{@pagebreak}
The first layer of the Mixer is built like a Wifi Symbol! First is Light Engineering Block, then Fluid Pipes, and Steel Scaffolding.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_mixer1.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Above our Light Engineering Block we'll put another and one to the left of the newly placed one. On the far right Scaffolding we'll place a Redstone Engineering Block. Then, we'll place a 2x2 of Iron Sheetmetal on the back of our Machine.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_mixer2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
On top of the third Light Engineering Block we'll place a singular Steel Fence, and to the right of it will be a fourth Light Engineering Block.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_mixer3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
To create the Mixer Right Click the Iron Sheetmetal between our Light Engineering Block and Redstone Engineering Block with a Engineer's Hammer!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_mixer.png width:100 height:100 align:center}

The Bottling Machine will fill up whatever Item comes by on the Belt. 

Use the Ports in the Back to fill the Machine with Fluids, you'll know it is working when the Tank is full of that Fluid! 

Then, when a Bucket, Tank, or any Fluid Storage comes down the Belt, it will be filled with that Fluid. 

The Bucket, Tank, or whatever will then move down the Belts full of that Fluid! 

By the way, like everything in life, the Bottling Machine will need Energy in the Ports at the Top of the Back side!
{@pagebreak}
To start, make a triangle out of Steel Scaffolding. Then fill the holes with Iron Sheetmetal, Redstone Engineering Block, and a Light Engineering Block.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_bottler1.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Now we just add a Conveyor Belt across the front side. Then, add a second Iron Sheetmetal on the other, a Fluid Pump next to it, and a Light Engineering Block on the previous one!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_bottler2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Simply Hammer the middle Conveyor Belt and BOOM done!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_bottler.png width:100 height:100 align:center}

The Fermenter will hold your Food Items and after awhile will form them into Ethanol. \n\nThere is a list of Items, you can find it in the Engineer's Manual, of Items that can be put into the Fermenter by the Ports in the Back and Left side. \n\nIf you use Honey Bottles, you can Extract the Bottles out from the Port on the Right Side. \n\nThe Fermenter will need Energy which will come from a Port on Top of the Fermenter!
{@pagebreak}
Pretty simple start, make a backwards n out of Steel Scaffolding and within it place Fluid Pipes and on the corner place a Light Engineering Block.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_fermenter1.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Above the Light Engineering Block place another. To the right of it, skip a Block, then place a Redstone Engineering Block. To the left of the Light Engineering Block we'll place a 2x2 of Cauldrons.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_fermenter2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Another simple step, just place Iron Sheetmetal above all the Cauldrons!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_fermenter3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Right Click the Cauldron between the Light Engineering Block and Redstone Engineering Block with a Hammer.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_fermenter.png width:100 height:100 align:center}

The Squeezer is a simple Machine that squeezes Items to make other Items or Fluids. \n\nWe can use the 2 Ports in the Back to Input Items. We'll then need to use the Port on the Right Side of the Barrels to take Items out. The Port below that one will Output Fluids. \n\nThis will mainly be used to squeeze Plant Oil out of Crop Seeds like Wheat Seeds or Hemp Seeds! \n\nSome Seeds give more Oil, check the Guide to see what each gives. \n\nWe'll also need to use the Squeezer to get HOP Graphite Dust from 8 Coke Dust.
{@pagebreak}
Literally the exact same start as the Fermenter.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_squeezer1.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Just like the Fermenter as well, just instead of Cauldrons use Barrels!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_squeezer2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Above the Barrel between the Light Engineering Block and Redstone Engineering Block place a Piston. On top of the other 3 Barrels place Steel Fence!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_squeezer3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Very easy Hammer Right Click on the Barrel beneath the Piston.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_squeezer.png width:100 height:100 align:center}

The Refinery will take 2 Fluids and combine and refine them into 1 better Fluid! \n\nThe 2 Fluids can be Input from the Ports and the Left and Right sides. The Fluid Output will come out the Front Port. \n\nYou can use Buckets to deposit Fluids into the Tanks as well! Don't forget to Right Click the Refinery to open its GUI. There we will need to place in a Catalyst, in order to start the Machine. \nAlong with a Catalyst, it'll need Energy which can be added via the Port in the Back!
{@pagebreak}
To start make a line of 5 Fluid Pipes. In the middle place Light Engineering Block on one side, and a Heavy Engineering Block on the other. Next to the rest of the Fluid Pipes place Steel Scaffolding.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_refinery1.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
Place more Engineering Blocks on the previous ones. To the right of the Heavy Engineering Block, skip 1 Block and place a Redstone Engineering Block. Next to the Light Engineering Block place 2 2x2 of Iron Sheetmetal.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_refinery2.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
Now just a few more Iron Sheetmetals!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_refinery3.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
For this one we'll need to Right Click the top Heavy Engineering Block with our Hammer.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_refinery.png width:100 height:100 align:center}

The Assembler, unlike most Machines, work mostly in its GUI. \n\nRight Click the Machine and set up 3 Recipes, by putting them into the Grids at the top of the screen. The order they are in, is the order it will follow for priority. \n\nYou can Input Items from the Belts and they will Output out of the back Belts. You can also Input Fluids which will be used to refill Buckets or Tanks used in Crafting! \n\nYou'll also need to power it with Energy from the Top.
{@pagebreak}
Place 2 parallel lines of 3 Steel Scaffolding with a Block of space in between them. Between them place a Light Engineering Block in the center, and Redstone Engineering Blocks around it.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_assembler1.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
On the sides with Redstone Engineering Blocks place Iron Sheetmetal. Then, above the Light Engineering Block we of course will need another. After, place Conveyor Belts going to and through the Light Engineering Block!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_assemble2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
This one might be confusing just be sight alone; place Iron Sheetmetal Slabs on our previously placed Iron Sheetmetal. Then, between them place full Iron Sheetmetal.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_assembler3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
To build our Assembler Right Click the first Conveyor Belt with our lovely Hammer!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_assembler.png width:100 height:100 align:center}

Another Multiblock that uses Belts, I'm seeing a pattern. First, we need to set a Blueprint. Right Click the Automated Workbench to open its GUI and place a Blueprint in the Right most slot. \n\nThen, we can have our Items go through the Belts to be used in Recipes if possible. \n\nAfter that, the Crafted Item (and Items that were accidentally put on the Belts) will go out the Belts. \n\nThis is useful for automating Bullets, HOP Graphite, and Mechanical Components.
{@pagebreak}
We start a lot of these with shapes using Steel Scaffolding, this time it is a diagonal line. On the smaller corner we'll place a Heavy Engineering Block. On the bigger corner we'll place 2 Light Engineering Blocks and a Redstone Engineering Block.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_automated1.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Next, we'll place more Light Engineering and Heavy Engineering Blocks on top of their former selves. Above the Redstone Engineering Block and the Steel Scaffolding to the left of it we'll place Treated Wood Slabs. Within the rest of the space we'll place Conveyor Belts in the order shown.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_automated2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
To get our Automated Workbench, smack the left Treated Wood Slab with the Engineer's Hammer!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_automated.png width:100 height:100 align:center}

The Arc Furnace is a massive and helpful Machine. It makes most other Machines useless! \n\nTo start you'll need Energy Input from the outlets in the Back of the Arc Furnace. It'll then need Fuel which are Graphite Electrodes. These can only be placed into its GUI, they can't be automated. \n\nYou'll then need to Input the Items into the Top Ports, near where the Graphite Electrodes are. When fueled and powered it'll melt down, just about anything. From Iron Rods to Iron Ingots, to Froststeel Helmets to Froststeel, to Gold Pickaxes to Gold! \n\nThe melted down Items will be Output into the Back below the Power Outlets. \n\nIt can also make Alloys from Metals!
{@pagebreak}
1st layer starts off with a U made of Steel Sheetmetal with the center being Heavy Engineering Block and the tips being Steel Blocks. The rest will be Steel Sheetmetal Slabs with a stray Steel Scaffolding and Cauldron.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_arc1.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
2nd layer starts with, above the Heavy Engineering Block and the 2 Blocks next to it will be Light Engineering Blocks. Then, the sides of the U will be Heavy Engineering Blocks. With more Steel Blocks above the previous ones. We'll also need a 2x3 of Reinforced Blast Bricks above the Slabs. Don't forget the Redstone Engineering Block above the Scaffolding!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_arc2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
3rd has more Steel Blocks, more Light Engineering Blocks, and an extension of our Reinforced Blast Bricks. We'll also need 1 Steel Sheetmetal on each side.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_arc3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
4th needs a Light Engineering Block placed in the middle above the others. Next to it will be 2 Steel Scaffolding. And we'll need to add more Reinforced Blast Brick but this time a Block of length short!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_arc4.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
5th and final layer is just 2 more Steel Scaffolding on top of the others. Then, Light Engineering Blocks above the previous one and in a line in front of it.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_arc5.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Finally Right Click the Cauldron with the Hammer to finish it!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_arc.png width:100 height:100 align:center}

What's that? It's only the hardest and most expensive Multiblock in Immersive Engineering. The Excavator! \n\nThis giant behemoth will automatically collect Ores and Blocks from the Ground. \n\nThe Items it picks up will be Output from a Port in the Back of it. If there's no Inventory next to it, it will dispense the Items. \n\nThis is also a super Energy hungry Machine, you'll need to use the Energy Ports on the Left Side of it to feed it!
{@pagebreak}
Place a Steel Block.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_excavator1.png width:100 height:100 align:center}
Add 3 Steel Scaffolding above the Steel Block and place 2 Steel Blocks on the ends.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_excavator2.png width:175 height:100 align:center}
After that place a 3x3 of Steel Scaffolding above the previous Scaffolding, and an extra one on each of the Steel Blocks. Then, using Steel Sheetmetal make a hoop off of the Scaffolding, including a Light Engineering Block and a Radiator Block.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_excavator3.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
Above the Steel Scaffolding add more, with a Steel Block in the middle. Then, attach more Steel Blocks to the ends of those. On one side it'll be 3 Light Engineering Blocks and the other will be 3 Heavy Engineering Blocks. Above the Light Engineering Block in the last layer, will be another. And above the Radiator Block will be a Redstone Engineering Block. Next to it will be another Heavy Engineering Block and the rest will be Steel Sheetmetal.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_excavator4.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
Now for the middle part we'll be repeating what we did below the half, so now it's just Steel Scaffolding. On the side next to it with Light Engineering Blocks will be 3 more, same with the random Light Engineering Block on the otherside. Next to the 3 Light Engineering Blocks will be 2 Radiator Blocks, and everything else is Sheetmetal.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/immersive/immersive_excavator5.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
Above the Steel Scaffolding will be 1 Steel Block followed by 3 Scaffolding and another Block.
