The Thermal Evaporation Plant is a Multiblock that takes Water, and uses Heat to make it into Brine. It will also use Heat to make Brine into Liquid Lithium! 

To start you'll need a lotta Thermal Evaporation Blocks. The base is 4x4 and only ever 4x4 of Thermal Evaporation Blocks. 

The Walls need to be atleast 3 Blocks tall and a max of 18. The inside and top must be hollow like most Multiblocks. The Water and Brine needs to be held somewhere. 

Within the Walls (not the corners) we can put our Valves and Controller! The Controller is how we access the Thermal Evaporation Plant's GUI. There we can see the Heat that is has. We'll only need 1 Controller. 

Valves are how we move Water and Brine in, Brine and Liquid Lithium out, and optionally Heat in! You won't need to configure the Valves, only the Pipes and Conductors need to be configured. 

The top layer of the Plant can't have the corners filled in with Thermal Evaporation Blocks. You can add Advanced Solar Generators on the corners of the top layer though if you want more Heat!
{@pagebreak}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/mek/mek_thermal1.png width:125 height:100 align:center}
Make a 4x4 of Thermal Blocks for the Base.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/mek/mek_thermal2.png width:125 height:100 align:center}
This part can be any size as long as the Thermal Evaporation Plant is between 3 Blocks and 18 Blocks Tall. It is also where we place our Valves and Controllers.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/mek/mek_thermal3.png width:110 height:100 align:center}
The Corners must be Empty or filled with Advanced Solar Generators on the Top Level.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/mek/mek_thermal4.png width:110 height:100 align:center}
You'll know it is set when the Controller lights up!

Teleporters will allow us to Teleport anywhere in any Dimension as long as the Machine is made and Powered! 

Now how do we make it and Power it? 

First, to make the Teleporter we'll need 1 Teleporter Block and 9 Teleporter Frames. 

The Teleporter Block is the main Controller of the Teleporter. It is the Block that will need Energy, and once Powered we can open it. Here we can set a Network similar to the Quantum Entangloporter, type in a name and click the Checkmark to make the Network! 

Now when other Teleporter Structures or Teleporter Blocks, are set to that Network (by clicking the named Network in their GUI) you can use the Teleporter to obviously Teleport to the other Teleporters at the same Network. 

Now about making the Teleporter Structure. Place a Teleporter Frame on each side of the Teleporter Block. Above those place 3 more to make it 4 Blocks high. With 2 Blocks space above the Teleporter Block, you can place our last Teleporter Frames. 

Now when Powered and set, the Teleporter will be ready and you can walk through whatever colored Portal spawned! 

(You can change the Color for each in the Teleporter GUI!)
{@pagebreak}
{image:atm:textures/questpics/mek/meka_portal1.png width:200 height:75 align:center}
Place the Teleporter Block with 2 Teleporter Frames next to it.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/mek/meka_portal2.png width:150 height:125 align:center}
Now place Teleporter Frames on the previous ones.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/mek/meka_portal3.png width:100 height:125 align:center}
Repeat.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/mek/meka_portal4.png width:100 height:140 align:center}
Now, we'll need a whole row of Teleporter Frames for the top.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/mek/meka_portal5.png width:110 height:150 align:center}
Once everything is set, the Portal of your choosing should appear like so!

Some Machines from Mekanism can be Upgraded like the Metallurgic Infuser and Enrichment Chamber. Some can't though, these can only take Upgrade Cards. \nThe ATM Devs saw this and wanted Players to instead of making 50 Electrolytic Separators they can make 1 Multiblock! \n\nIn order to Craft these Multiblocks though, we'll need a previous Multiblock. The Automatic Hepheastus Forge. \n\nIt has its own Quest in Chapter 4: Creative. Check it out there! \n\nAll of the Multiblocks use the same Structure just with different Controllers. Check out the Next Page in order to see Instructions on Building it!
{@pagebreak}
The first layer is the most complicated with it hosting all of the Machine Casings. The various Machine Casings will be within the middle while the Darkstone Stairs and Blocks and Gilded Chiseled Polished Darkstone surrounds them.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/mek/mek_multi_runic1.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
The second layer tops off the first with more Darkstone Bricks and Stairs. Now it includes Darkstone Slabs and Rune Blocks as well!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/mek/mek_multi_runic2.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
Doesn't get more simple than this! Just place Darkstone Pillars above the 4 outer Rune Blocks and that's all you have to do!
{image:atm:textures/questpics/mek/mek_multi_runic3.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
I was right, it doesn't get more simple. It just stays the same exact amount of simple! Repeat the previous step.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/mek/mek_multi_runic4.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
To finish, place Arcane Crystal Blocks above the Darkstone Pillars and a Quantum Injector above the uncovered Rune Block.
{image:atm:textures/questpics/mek/mek_multi_runic5.png width:150 height:100 align:center}
Our Multiblock Machines will need Hatches to work though! To add them, replace the Darkstone Bricks on the first layer with the Hatches.

