First, we build. Second, we start up. Third, we use. 

All sides of the Fusion Reactor use a 5 Block long Diamond shape. The frame will be made of Fusion Reactor Casing and the inside can be made of Reactor Glass. 

The Fusion Reactor Ports can replace any Reactor Glass Block in the Structure (besides where other Blocks are needed) 

The Laser Focus Matrix will also be placed where Reactor Glass is. Hopefully not to close to other Blocks though! 

The Fusion Reactor Controller, the most important Block, will be placed in the square center of the top layer. 

Don't worry the inside will be hollow... I don't recommend checking if it is when it's on, that'll kill you.
{@pagebreak}
BOOM! It is built! Now how do we get this puppy working? 

First, grab your Hohlraum, which should be filled! And place it within the GUI of the Fusion Reactor. 

We can open its GUI by Right Clicking the Controller of a fully built one. 

Now along with the filled Hohlraum we'll need to throw some Fuel in! 

Then, we can blast the Laser Amplifier with atleast 1GFE, into the Laser Focus Matrix. 

Now it is ready for use!
{@pagebreak}
Most of the use is through the Controller. First, we get the main menu. This is just for the Hohlraum slot, and telling you if it is built correctly! 

Next, is the Heat menu. This is for how Hot the Temperature of the Fusion Reactor is. This determines the amount of Energy or Steam is created! And is determined by the Laser Amplifier being shot into it, and if it is cooled. 

We can change the Units of Temperature or even Energy with the bottom Buttons! 

Next menu, is for Fuel! It will show how much Deuterium, Tritium, and D-T Fuel is within the Fusion Reactor. We can also change the Inject Rate, how much Fuel is used up each Tick. 

Stats menu shows us a lot of fancy numbers! They're only important to nerds so we won't focus on them!
{@pagebreak}
