The Thermoelectric Boiler is built similar to the Fission Reactor with the outside shell being just Casings, Glass, and Ports, while the inside is all the important stuff! 

The edges of the Boiler will need to be Boiler Casings. The Roof and Floor can be made entirely of Casings or the middle can be made with Glass! 

The Walls are similar, just now including Boiler Ports. 

The inside is where our Pressure Dispersers and Superheating Elements. 
The Roof can be given space between the Ceiling and the Pressure Dispersers to give more room for Steam. 

We can also give more space below the Pressure Dispersers and above the Superheating Elements to give more room for Water.
{@pagebreak}
The Thermoelectric Boiler won't do much on its own, it'll need some Ports moving our Chemicals and Fluids in to start it up! 

Right now we'll focus on cooling Superheated Sodium! For that we'll need Superheated Sodium and Water within the Boiler. 

Once the Superheated Sodium is in, the Boiler's Temperature will start rising. With the Water the Superheated Sodium will cool down while the Water will boil into Steam. 

The higher the Temperature the quicker Water will boil and Superheated Sodium will cool down. If we want/need extra Heat we can Conduct some via the Thermodynamic Conductors. 

We can Conduct Heat from Resistive Heaters or even Fission Reactors!
{@pagebreak}
