We're going to build the smallest passive reactor possible, the 3x3x3. The requirements for the quest are the exact amounts for what you'll need to build one.

To build this, you start by building a 3x3x3 frame made out of Casings. In the middle of the bottom face, you can just use another Reactor Casing. You'll want each outer wall to have a reactor component, like an Active Power Tap or Solid Access Port.
{@pagebreak}
Every reactor you build will require exactly 1 Reactor Controller, which is usually put in the middle of the front wall. Next, we'll place 1 Fuel Rod in the center of the multiblock, and 1 Control Rod above it on the top face.

You will need a way to input and output waste, which is done by using Reactor Solid Access Ports. For this build, place one on the left side and one on the right.

To extract power, we'll place the Active Power Tap on the middle of the back wall. Once placed, the reactor should complete! You can now right click the Controller to open up the interface and turn it on!

Note: The biggest reactor you can make using Basic Reactor Parts is 5x5x5. To build a larger reactor, you will need Reinforced Reactor Parts.
{@pagebreak}
This is what a 3x3x3 reactor will look like:

{image:atm:textures/questpics/extremereactors/3x3sample.png width:150 height:150 align:1}

To insert fuel into the reactor, you'll need to pick one of the sides that has a Reactor Solid Access Port and pump in Uranium from an inventory.

The easiest way to do this is to use something like a Storage Drawer or even just a Chest with an Item Pipe connected at the top, like the image shown below.

{image:atm:textures/questpics/extremereactors/importexample.png width:150 height:150 align:1}

To build the frame for the Reprocessor, you'll need a lot of Casings. This also means a lot of Cyanite.

Start by building a hollow 3 block wide, 3 block deep, and 7 block tall structure. This is the frame.

If done right, you'll have an empty spot in the middle of the bottom and top face. For the vertical faces, you can either use Reprocessor Glass or one of the required Reprocessor parts like the Power Port, Controller, etc.

